  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the equation <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. The number of different values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> so that the given equation has integral roots, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> will be a perfect square,</p><p>&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> is a perfect square<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>36</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>49</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>81</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>100</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>35</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>48</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>63</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>80</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>99</mn></math><br />Therefore,&nbsp;<math><mn>8</mn></math> values are possible.</p>",
